WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.894
EDR is powerful, but it is not magic.

2
00:00:02.894 --> 00:00:09.788
It can be misconfigured, ignored, bypassed, overwhelmed by alerts, or limited by poor coverage.

3
00:00:09.788 --> 00:00:16.922
If endpoints are unmanaged, offline, excluded, or not sending telemetry, defenders may have blind spots.

4
00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:25.194
EDR works best when it is deployed broadly, tuned carefully, monitored consistently, and connected to incident response processes.

5
00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:41.268
Good practices include maintaining endpoint coverage, reviewing high-value alerts, tuning noisy detections, documenting response procedures, integrating with SIEM or SOAR where appropriate, and training analysts to investigate endpoint behavior.

6
00:00:41.268 --> 00:00:44.670
EDR is one layer in a defense-in-depth strategy.

7
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:55.047
It does not replace patching, identity security, network monitoring, backups, user awareness, secure configuration, or incident response planning.

8
00:00:55.047 --> 00:01:01.642
Its value comes from reliable visibility, useful detections, practiced response, and human judgment.
